# .cursorrules — CallContext Development Rules
# Place this file in your project root. Cursor reads it automatically.

## Project Overview
CallContext is a real-time call intelligence CRM for small shop owners (florists first, then bakeries, salons, etc). It captures phone calls via Vonage, transcribes them live with Deepgram, extracts entities with GPT-4o-mini, and auto-builds customer profiles, reminders, and orders.

## Project Documentation
All project documentation lives in the `docs/` folder at the project root. ALWAYS reference these before building any feature:
- `docs/engineering-plan.md` — 22-week build plan with every page, endpoint, table, and test
- `docs/features.md` — Full 200+ feature brainstorm with priorities (P0–P3)
- `docs/architecture.md` — Scalable 4-layer architecture, scaling milestones, security model
- `docs/design-system.md` — Colors, typography, components, animations, Tailwind config
- `docs/project-setup.md` — Step-by-step project initialization guide

When asked to build a feature, check the engineering plan first for exact specs, then the design system for UI patterns.

