### Key Architecture Decisions
- **Frontend** (Next.js on Vercel): Handles all UI rendering, auth, lightweight API routes (CRUD operations, Stripe/Vonage webhooks). Serverless — auto-scales, no servers to manage.
- **Backend** (Node.js/Go on Railway): Handles ONLY stateful real-time work — WebSocket audio streaming, Deepgram transcription, AI extraction, live dashboard push. This is the only server you manage.
- **Database** (Supabase): Shared by both frontend and backend. Frontend uses Supabase client SDK with RLS. Backend uses direct connection for writes during calls.
- **The split is clean**: Frontend does request-response. Backend does streaming. They share the database but never talk to each other directly.

## Tech Stack

### Frontend (DO NOT deviate)
- Framework: Next.js 16+ (App Router, NOT Pages Router)
- Language: TypeScript (strict mode)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 (theme defined via @theme in globals.css, NOT tailwind.config.ts)
- Database client: Supabase JS SDK (@supabase/ssr)
- Data fetching: SWR (client-side), Server Components (server-side)
- Icons: Lucide React
- Charts: Recharts
- Validation: Zod
- Payments: Stripe (@stripe/stripe-js)
- Email: Resend

### Backend (may evolve)
- Starting: Node.js + TypeScript + Express + ws library
- May migrate to: Go (Golang) + Fiber/Chi + gorilla/websocket
- Transcription: Deepgram Nova-3 SDK (streaming WebSocket)
- AI: OpenAI GPT-4o-mini
- Database: Supabase (direct PostgreSQL connection via pgx if Go, or @supabase/supabase-js if Node)
- Logging: pino (Node) or zerolog (Go)

### Shared
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + Realtime + Storage)
- Telephony: Vonage Voice API
- Hosting: Vercel (frontend) + Railway (backend)
- Monitoring: Sentry (both) + PostHog (frontend)

## Frontend Rules

### Routing
- Use Next.js App Router route groups: (auth), (dashboard), (onboarding), (marketing)
- Dashboard layout wraps all protected pages with sidebar + header
- Auth pages have a clean layout with no sidebar
- API routes go in callcontext-frontend/app/api/[feature]/route.ts

### Data Fetching
- Server Components for initial page data (default)
- Client Components ('use client') only when needed for interactivity
- SWR for client-side data fetching with caching
- Supabase Realtime for live updates (calls, screen pops)
- NEVER fetch data in useEffect — use Server Components or SWR

### API Routes (in frontend)
- Handle: auth, CRUD operations, Vonage/Stripe webhooks, cron jobs, exports
- Every route: auth check → input validation (Zod) → business logic → response
- Always verify shop_id from auth context
- Return consistent JSON: { data } on success, { error: string } on failure
- Always return 200 for Vonage webhooks (they retry on non-200)
- Use Supabase server client with service role for webhooks

### What the frontend API does NOT handle
- Long-lived WebSocket connections (Vercel times out at 30s)
- Audio streaming from Vonage
- Deepgram real-time transcription
- AI entity extraction during calls
- Any process that needs to stay alive for more than 30 seconds
- These all live in the backend (Railway)

## Backend Rules

### Responsibilities (backend ONLY handles these)
1. Vonage audio WebSocket — receive PCM audio stream for duration of call
2. Deepgram streaming — forward audio, receive live transcript fragments
3. Dashboard WebSocket — push live transcript + entities to browser
4. AI extraction — batch transcript every 30s → GPT-4o-mini → entities
5. Post-call analysis — full summary + profile update when call ends
6. Database writes — save transcript, update customer, create orders/reminders

### Connection Management
```
Per active call, backend holds:
  - 1 WebSocket from Vonage (audio in)
  - 1 WebSocket to Deepgram (audio out, transcript in)
  - N WebSockets to dashboard tabs (transcript + entities out)

Total memory per call: ~5-10KB
At 100 concurrent calls: ~1MB
Bottleneck is WebSocket count, not memory
```

### If Migrating to Go
- Keep the same WebSocket message format (JSON) so frontend doesn't change
- Keep the same Supabase table writes so data layer doesn't change
- Keep the same Deepgram SDK integration pattern
- Benefits: goroutines handle 10x more concurrent calls per instance, lower memory, faster audio processing
- Migrate ONLY when Node.js performance becomes the bottleneck (likely at 200+ concurrent calls)

## Design System (FOLLOW EXACTLY)

### Colors — Tailwind Custom Config
```
Brand:     brand-50 through brand-900 (teal green, primary: brand-500 #2D8F6F)
Accent:    accent-50 through accent-900 (warm amber, primary: accent-400 #F5AD1F)
Neutrals:  warm-25 through warm-900 (warm grays, NOT cool blue-grays)
Semantic:  success/warning/danger/info with -50 and -500 and -700 stops

Full specs in docs/design-system.md
```

### Typography
- Font sans: 'DM Sans' (body, UI, everything)
- Font display: 'Outfit' (headings, page titles, stat numbers)
- Font mono: 'JetBrains Mono' (phone numbers, timestamps, IDs)
- Base size: 14px (text-sm in Tailwind = 13px for secondary text)
- Dashboard greeting: font-display text-3xl font-semibold
- Page titles: font-display text-2xl font-semibold
- Body text: text-sm (14px) text-warm-700
- Secondary text: text-xs (13px) text-warm-500

### Component Patterns
- Buttons: rounded-md, h-9 default, transitions all 150ms
  - Primary: bg-brand-500 text-white hover:bg-brand-600
  - Secondary: bg-white border border-warm-200 hover:bg-warm-50
  - Ghost: bg-transparent hover:bg-warm-100
  - Danger: bg-red-500 text-white hover:bg-red-700
- Inputs: h-9, border-warm-200, rounded-md, focus:ring-brand-500
- Cards: bg-white border border-warm-200 rounded-lg p-5 shadow-sm
- Badges: rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium
  - Success: bg-success-50 text-success-700 border border-green-200
  - Warning: bg-warning-50 text-warning-700
  - Danger: bg-danger-50 text-danger-700
- Tags: rounded-full px-2.5 py-0.5 text-xs bg-brand-50 text-brand-700 border border-brand-200
- Avatars: rounded-full, initials on bg-brand-100 text-brand-600
- Tables: header bg-warm-50 text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-warm-500
- Modals: backdrop-blur-sm bg-black/40, modal bg-white rounded-xl shadow-xl

### Spacing
- Page padding: p-6 (24px)
- Card padding: p-5 (20px)
- Between sections: space-y-6
- Between cards in grid: gap-4
- Between form fields: space-y-4

### Responsive
- Sidebar: 240px fixed on desktop (lg+), collapsed to icons on tablet (md), bottom nav on mobile
- Stat cards: grid-cols-4 lg, grid-cols-2 md, grid-cols-1 sm
- Tables: overflow-x-auto on mobile, or switch to card layout

### Animations
- Hover transitions: transition-all duration-150
- Page enter: animate-in fade-in slide-in-from-bottom-2 duration-200
- Screen pop: animate-in slide-in-from-top duration-400
- Entity detected: animate-in slide-in-from-right duration-400
- Loading skeleton: animate-pulse with warm-100 to warm-150 gradient
- Pulse dot (live call): custom animation 2s ease-in-out infinite

### Icons
- Use Lucide React exclusively
- Size: 16px inline, 20px nav, 24px feature cards
- Stroke width: 1.5 (default)
- Color: text-warm-400 (secondary), text-warm-700 (primary), text-white (on buttons)

## Code Style

### TypeScript (both frontend and backend)
- Strict mode enabled
- Define interfaces for all API inputs/outputs
- Use Zod schemas for runtime validation
- Export types from lib/types/database.ts (auto-generated from Supabase)
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes
- Use `as const` for constant arrays and objects

### React Components (frontend only)
- Functional components only
- Use named exports (not default) for non-page components
- Props interface defined above component
- Destructure props in function signature
- Keep components under 150 lines — extract sub-components
- Use composition over prop drilling

### Naming
- Components: PascalCase (CustomerProfile.tsx)
- Hooks: camelCase with use prefix (useWebSocket.ts)
- Utils: camelCase (formatPhone.ts)
- API routes: kebab-case directories (api/vonage/answer/route.ts)
- Database columns: snake_case
- TypeScript interfaces: PascalCase with descriptive names (CustomerWithCalls)
- Enums: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE values
- Go files (if adopted): snake_case (audio_handler.go)
- Go packages: lowercase single word (websocket, transcription, ai)

### Error Handling
- API routes: try/catch, return appropriate status codes
- Client: SWR error states, toast notifications for user-facing errors
- Never show raw error messages to users
- Log errors with context (shop_id, call_id, user_id)
- Vonage webhooks: ALWAYS return 200, log errors separately
- Backend: structured logging with pino (Node) or zerolog (Go)

### Security (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
- RLS enabled on EVERY Supabase table
- Auth check on EVERY frontend API route (except webhooks)
- Zod validation on EVERY API input
- Never expose SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY to client/browser
- Never expose API keys in client-side code
- Use signed URLs for recording access (1hr expiry)
- Parameterized queries only (Supabase handles this)
- NEVER use dangerouslySetInnerHTML
- Backend WebSocket: verify shop_id from headers before accepting connection
- Backend dashboard WebSocket: verify Supabase JWT before accepting

## Supabase Patterns

### Client-Side (browser — frontend only)
```typescript
import { createBrowserClient } from '@supabase/ssr'
export const supabase = createBrowserClient(
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL!,
  process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY!
)
```

### Server-Side (API routes, Server Components — frontend only)
```typescript
import { createServerClient } from '@supabase/ssr'
import { cookies } from 'next/headers'
// Use for authenticated operations — respects RLS
```

### Service Role (webhooks, cron, backend server)
```typescript
import { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js'
// Use for operations that need to bypass RLS
// Used in: Vonage webhooks, cron jobs, Railway backend
// NEVER use in client-side / browser code
```

### Realtime Subscriptions (frontend)
```typescript
supabase
  .channel('channel-name')
  .on('postgres_changes', { event: 'INSERT', schema: 'public', table: 'calls', filter: `shop_id=eq.${shopId}` }, callback)
  .subscribe()
```

## Common Patterns

### Frontend Page Layout
```tsx
// Server Component page (callcontext-frontend/app/(dashboard)/customers/page.tsx)
export default async function CustomersPage() {
  const supabase = await createClient()
  const { data } = await supabase.from('customers').select('*').order('last_contact_date', { ascending: false })
  return (
    <div className="space-y-6">
      <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
        <h1 className="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-warm-800">Customers</h1>
        <Button>Add customer</Button>
      </div>
      <CustomerTable initialData={data} />
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Frontend API Route
```tsx
// callcontext-frontend/app/api/customers/route.ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from 'next/server'
import { z } from 'zod'

const schema = z.object({ name: z.string().min(1) })

export async function POST(req: NextRequest) {
  try {
    const supabase = await createClient()
    const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser()
    if (!user) return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 })

    const body = await req.json()
    const parsed = schema.safeParse(body)
    if (!parsed.success) return NextResponse.json({ error: parsed.error.flatten() }, { status: 400 })

    const { data, error } = await supabase.from('customers').insert(parsed.data).select().single()
    if (error) throw error

    return NextResponse.json(data, { status: 201 })
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error:', error)
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Internal server error' }, { status: 500 })
  }
}
```

### Frontend Client Component with SWR
```tsx
'use client'
import useSWR from 'swr'

const fetcher = (url: string) => fetch(url).then(r => r.json())

export function CustomerList({ initialData }: { initialData: Customer[] }) {
  const { data, error, isLoading } = useSWR('/api/customers', fetcher, { fallbackData: initialData })

  if (isLoading) return <Skeleton />
  if (error) return <ErrorState />
  if (!data?.length) return <EmptyState />

  return <Table data={data} />
}
```

### Backend WebSocket Handler (Node.js)
```typescript
// backend/src/websocket/audioHandler.ts
export function handleAudioStream(ws: WebSocket, shopId: string, callId: string) {
  const dgConnection = openDeepgramStream()

  ws.on('message', (audio: Buffer) => {
    dgConnection.send(audio)
  })

  dgConnection.on('transcript', (data) => {
    pushToDashboard(shopId, callId, { type: 'transcript', ...data })
  })

  ws.on('close', () => {
    dgConnection.finish()
    runPostCallAnalysis(shopId, callId)
  })
}
```

### Backend WebSocket Handler (Go — if migrated)
```go
// backend/websocket/audio_handler.go
func HandleAudioStream(conn *websocket.Conn, shopID, callID string) {
    dgConn := openDeepgramStream()
    defer dgConn.Close()

    for {
        _, audio, err := conn.ReadMessage()
        if err != nil {
            break
        }
        dgConn.Send(audio)
    }

    runPostCallAnalysis(shopID, callID)
}
```

## What NOT to do

### Frontend
- Do NOT use Pages Router (App Router only)
- Do NOT use Redux, Zustand, or Jotai (SWR + context is enough)
- Do NOT use CSS modules or styled-components (Tailwind only)
- Do NOT use any UI library (shadcn, MUI, Chakra) — build from design system
- Do NOT hardcode colors — use Tailwind config custom colors
- Do NOT use localStorage for auth tokens (Supabase uses cookies)
- Do NOT use `any` type — define proper types
- Do NOT skip Zod validation on API inputs
- Do NOT use `useEffect` for data fetching
- Do NOT create API routes for things Supabase can do directly (auth, realtime)
- Do NOT put WebSocket or streaming logic in frontend API routes (use backend)

### Backend
- Do NOT serve HTML or frontend assets from the backend
- Do NOT duplicate auth logic — backend trusts shop_id from Vonage headers or JWT verification
- Do NOT store state between requests (except active call state in memory)
- Do NOT use an ORM — use Supabase client or raw SQL via pgx
- Do NOT build a full REST API on the backend — CRUD lives in frontend API routes
- Do NOT skip structured logging — every call event must be logged

### Both
- Do NOT write raw SQL when Supabase query builder works
- Do NOT store secrets in code — environment variables only
- Do NOT skip error handling — every async operation needs try/catch or error callback
- Do NOT ignore the design system — refer to docs/design-system.md for every UI decision
- Do NOT build features not in the current week's plan — check docs/engineering-plan.md
